/*
 * Declares the MapIteratorValueAccessValue class.
 *
 * MapIteratorValueAccessValue represents the operation that retrieves the value
 * associated with the current position of a map iterator. This is the value
 * counterpart to MapIteratorKeyValue, and is used during iteration to access
 * the mapped value of the entry the iterator currently points to.
 *
 * The iterator must refer to a valid entry; retrieving a value when the
 * iterator is at the end position is undefined.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::map::iteration::value
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/map/iteration/value.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-11-15
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
